# The Colibrì Stage 2A bounded converter is pinned by an immutable
# reviewed SHA-256 in colibri_stage2_common.REVIEWED_BOUNDED_CONVERTER_IDENTITY
# and is re-verified immediately before every subprocess launch. Its
# checked-out bytes must therefore be identical on every platform and in
# every clone.
#
# Without this rule the repository's core.autocrlf=true would rewrite the
# file's line endings on checkout: a fresh clone produces 24,670 CRLF
# bytes while a Linux checkout produces 24,033 LF bytes, so no single
# pinned hash could ever match both. Forcing LF makes the working-tree
# bytes equal the stored blob bytes exactly, which is what the pinned
# digest is computed over.
python/odysseus_desktop_backend/services/colibri_stage2_bounded_convert.py text eol=lf
